window.docContents[239].resolve({"/Ideals-and-splitting/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Ideals-and-splitting":{"contents":"\n\nFor primes  dividing , the ideals  and\n in  have\ncoordinate membership criteria.\n\nThose concrete ideals have quotient\ndescriptions by , which supply the primality proofs.\n\nThe quotient descriptions prove that both ideals are\nprime in the relevant concrete splitting branch.\n\nThe stable splitting API packages split, inert, and ramified behavior for primes\nin quadratic number fields, building on\nthe ring-of-integers classification.\n\nFor odd primes not dividing the parameter,\nsplitting and inertia are controlled by\nthe Legendre symbol.\n\nThe prime  is handled by the expected congruences modulo  and modulo\n, completing the\ntrichotomy at the even prime.\n\nThe  examples verify ideal factorizations above \nand , serving as concrete tests of\nthe ideal-primality API and\nthe splitting classification.\n\nA future cleanup should unify\nthe odd-prime and\ntwo-adic splitting statements using a\nKronecker-symbol formulation where that abstraction is helpful.\n\n","context":"Quadratic Number Fields Blueprint","header":"5. Ideals and splitting","id":"/Ideals-and-splitting/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Ideals-and-splitting"}});